    the schema 16 -> 17 rung is minted: the first rung since 8 whose subject is the CORPUS, and the first since 12 that moves rows
    
    RULED for lane OSR-SCHEMA17. The previous car moved a governed DETECTOR SOURCE, which
    darkens the plain gate BY DESIGN — it returns 1 without scanning at all. `--write` cannot
    absorb that and must not: frozen numbers taken under one detector do not mean the same thing
    under another. A rung is the only lawful road, and this car is the LAW that admits it. The
    re-freeze is the next car, exactly as at 15 -> 16.
    
    ── CONDITION 1: THE DELTA IS MEASURED, AND IT IS A FIXED POINT ─────────────────────────
    
    Derived by hashing each of the ELEVEN governed detector inputs against the PREDECESSOR'S OWN
    RECORDED MANIFEST — not against HEAD, and not by reasoning about which files I touched:
    
      MOVED (4):     scripts/check-observed-shape-readers.mjs
                     scripts/lib/observed-shape-baseline.mjs
                     scripts/lib/observed-shape-corpus.mjs      <- THE SUBJECT
                     scripts/migrate-observed-shape-readers.mjs
      BYTE-SAME (7): package.json · package-lock.json · governed-artifact-io.mjs ·
                     legacy-reader-shape-scan.mjs · observed-shape-governance.mjs ·
                     reader-shape-scan.mjs · spatialPackFixtures.js
    
    ⭐ RE-MEASURED AFTER THE SET WAS WRITTEN, because writing it changes
    `migrate-observed-shape-readers.mjs`, which is itself a member: declared == measured, still
    four. A mis-declared delta set is how rung 10->11 became permanently unmigratable.
    
    ⛔ FOUR RATHER THAN THREE, and the extra one is the whole rung: 13->14, 15->16 moved three
    because their subject was already one of the three bookkeeping files. This subject is a
    detector input that is NOT, so it adds itself. `package.json` and `package-lock.json` are
    MEASURED byte-same, not asserted: any package.json byte is itself a mint trigger.
    
    ── WHAT MAKES THIS RUNG DIFFERENT FROM THE LAST FOUR ───────────────────────────────────
    
    13, 14, 15 and 16 were VERDICT-ONLY: the door's validator moved, the detector's alphabet did
    not, and each had to report a row delta of ZERO. This one is the opposite kind and says so in
    its own header: the DETECTOR's reach moved, and rows move with it.
    
      identities 1409 -> 1397 · findings 1993 -> 1972 · files 388 -> 386
      GONE 12 · NEW 0 · RAISED 0 · LOWERED 0
    
    ⛔ THE FENCE THAT MATTERS IS THE ZERO ON `new`/`increased`, NOT THE TWELVE. The migration
    report raises issues for `new` and `increased` only — `gone` is a lawful shrink needing no
    discharge — so a single ADDED identity would mean the corpus grew its JUDGEMENT rather than
    its OBSERVATION, and the mint stops. Measured through the gate's own declared post-scan chain
    reproduced out of band, because a moved detector source leaves no in-band way to look first.
    The reproduction was VALIDATED BEFORE IT WAS TRUSTED: at the unchanged tree it reproduces the
    frozen register identity-for-identity and count-for-count, and reproduces the frozen
    `corpusMeta` in all nine fields.
    
    ── THE SHAPE FOLLOWS 15->16, THE CLOSEST PRECEDENT. Deviations: none. ───────────────────
    
    Every move is a data row in a table that already existed:
      · `STRESS_TOPOLOGY_TARGET_SCHEMA = 17`
      · `LEAF_MIGRATION_PREDECESSOR[17] = 16`          (chain stays SINGLE-STEP)
      · `LEAF_PREDECESSOR_VALIDATOR[16] = validateSchema16Baseline`, re-bound to its own
        RETIRED literal so a schema-16 predecessor is still validated as 16
      · `SCANNER_TRANSITION_BY_TARGET[17]` with the measured `deltaPaths`
      · `RETIRED_COMPANION_GATE_BASELINE_SCHEMA = 16`, `BASELINE_SCHEMA = 17`,
        `validateSchema17Baseline` minted and the checker's three bindings moved to it
      · header rationale paragraphs in the voice every prior rung uses
    
    ── THE ENUMERATED PINS THAT MOVED WITH THE RUNG, EACH FOR ITS OWN STATED REASON ────────
    
      · `BASELINE_SCHEMA` pins 16 -> 17 (baseline x1, sentinel x2)
      · the exact `LEAF_MIGRATION_PREDECESSOR` table gains `17: 16`
      · `validateSchema16Baseline` is paired with a NEW schema-16 fixture rather than with
        `live`, which now belongs to 17 — the same move every rung makes
      · ⭐ BOTH OUT-OF-TABLE PROBES MOVE UP A RUNG (17 -> 18), which the tests' OWN comments
        prescribe: a probe left pointing at a number the table has since adopted "stops proving
        the predicate is total and starts proving nothing at all, while still passing for the
        wrong reason"
    
    ── ⭐ AND FIVE WALKER PINS THAT MOVE BECAUSE THE BANK SHRANK ───────────────────────────
    
    The two banked `isCriminal on incomeSources` addresses (EconomicsTab.jsx, treasury.js) are
    DELETED by this shrink: their reads stopped being findings once the corpus could observe the
    writer. So the bank goes 64/43 -> 62/41, the live banked count 64 -> 62, the banked ROSTER
    9 -> 8, both per-identity maps read `{ reads: 0, addresses: 0 }`, and the A7 mutant's
    arithmetic follows. ⭐ The DECLARED roster is still NINE: banked ⊆ declared, and a
    declaration that banks nothing is a thing this arm should be able to say out loud.
    ⚠ The tree-shaped triple needed no edit — it reads `registerFigures()` off the register,
    which is the repair a previous lane landed for exactly this event.
    
    ⛔ AND THE EXEMPTION'S OWN RECORDED `why` WAS FALSIFIED BY THIS RUNG, SO IT IS CORRECTED
    RATHER THAN LEFT STANDING. It read "MEASURED: the corpus observed 3,068 incomeSources rows
    and NOT ONE carried isCriminal … dead on generated worlds by construction". The count was
    true; the conclusion was the corpus speaking for the code. It now records both readings and
    the 39-row difference between them, which is this rung's stress pass exactly — an arithmetic
    cross-check I did not plant: 3,068 + 39 = 3,107. The `ruling` field is untouched, because it
    is history and because a tag reason is append-only without numeric growth.
    
    ⚠ KNOWN RED, CARRIED DELIBERATELY: the baseline is still schema 16 with a drifted detector,
    so the plain gate returns 1 ("expected 17 … build and review the governed migration bundle")
    and the walker's SHRINK-ONLY and bank arms red until the next car's re-freeze. No register
    act in this car; no `.json` baseline touched.
    
